# Striatum Agent Guide (Gemini CLI profile)

This guide is intended for Gemini CLI. Load it as system context
before driving a striatum workflow — paste it into the system
prompt, or use your CLI's "include this Markdown as a tool input"
convention. The content is structurally identical to the generic
profile; the dedicated filename keeps `striatum skills install
--profile all` collision-free.

When Gemini CLI's skill-discovery convention stabilizes, the
`gemini` profile will graduate to a five-file shape matching
Claude Code; until then, this single guide is the canonical answer.

Striatum is a local-first runner whose authoritative live state
lives in a daemon-owned PostgreSQL instance under a `repository_id`
scope per target repository (D094 / RFC 0043). `.striatum/` next to
the target repo is operational scratch only. The runner — not your
prose, and not direct database access — advances state.

## Scaffold

Bring a target repo from "no `.striatum/`" to "a run that's ready
to claim work":

{verbs_scaffold}

Common pattern:

```bash
striatum --repo /path/to/target init
striatum --repo /path/to/target workflow validate path/to/workflow.json
striatum --repo /path/to/target run prepare --workflow path/to/workflow.json --json
striatum --repo /path/to/target run start --run-id <id> --json
```

## Claim loop

The core verb sequence for actually doing work:

{verbs_claim_loop}

Common pattern:

```bash
striatum --repo $REPO register-session --run-id $RUN \
    --role $ROLE --lane $LANE --json
striatum --repo $REPO claim-next --session-id $SESSION --json
striatum --repo $REPO ack --session-id $SESSION \
    --message-id $MSG --lease-id $LEASE --json
striatum --repo $REPO publish-artifact --session-id $SESSION \
    --job-id $JOB --lease-id $LEASE \
    --kind $KIND --logical-name $NAME --path $PATH --json
striatum --repo $REPO complete --session-id $SESSION \
    --job-id $JOB --lease-id $LEASE --json
```

For review jobs, do not call `complete`. Replace the last two steps with
`submit-review --verdict {{accept,accept_with_findings,needs_revision,reject}}`;
the daemon rejects bare completion for verdict-capable jobs.

